{
  "topic": "mathematics of juggling",
  "slug": "mathematics-of-juggling",
  "created": "2026-08-20",
  "student_level": "intermediate",
  "prerequisites": [
    "Combinatorics: permutations, binomial coefficients, generating functions, bijective proof techniques",
    "Modular arithmetic and basic number theory",
    "Linear algebra: matrices, eigenvalues, matrix powers, stochastic matrices",
    "Probability: sample spaces, conditional probability, expectation, introductory Markov chains",
    "Proof fluency: mathematical induction, construction, contradiction, and reading published proofs",
    "Elementary group theory: groups, subgroups, homomorphisms, group actions"
  ],
  "exit_criteria": [
    "Determine the validity of any siteswap sequence using both the average theorem and the permutation test",
    "Construct and analyze the complete state transition graph for b balls with a given maximum throw height",
    "State and prove the (b+1)^p counting theorem for juggling sequences via bijection",
    "Identify primitive juggling sequences and decompose composite siteswaps into their primitive components",
    "Model random juggling as a Markov chain on states and derive the stationary distribution using Stirling numbers",
    "Read and follow the core arguments in Buhler et al. (1994) and Warrington (2003) independently",
    "Construct the braid word corresponding to a periodic siteswap and identify the resulting link type",
    "Explain the correspondence between bounded affine permutations and positroid varieties in the Grassmannian"
  ],
